# /score-entities

Generalizes Topwater's `/score-companies`. Scores every discovered
{{vocabulary.entity}} against `originate.config.json`'s `criteria` block —
before a single dollar is spent on enrichment.

---

## Before anything

Load `standards/OUTPUT-STANDARDS.md` Rule O4 (reuse — unit is the
{{vocabulary.entity}}; a {{vocabulary.entity}} with no row in the prior
scored file is the only "new" work) and Rule O1 (checkpointing below
depends on this skill's own run folder existing before scoring starts).

## Checkpointing (this is the batch-level layer named in
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` §3 — implement it here, not elsewhere)

Score in small batches. As each batch finishes, save it to its own
checkpoint file immediately — never held until the whole run completes. If
a run is interrupted and picked back up, the next attempt reads whatever
checkpoint files already exist, treats those {{vocabulary.entityPlural}} as
done, and only re-does the batch that was actually still in progress. This
is what makes a large run (hundreds of {{vocabulary.entityPlural}}) safe to
interrupt without losing finished work.

